{"seq":21,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T13:18:43.375Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"76e6b0e771e97f66795c4c5124bccb70a193c3896f034940a3dcbc1c7b9e8513","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes (the North team digests):\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Eau Claire, Dock Doors 14–18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through fine. The note also says to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other North digests that mention QFL (9/14 pipeline and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in) don't have any ticket numbers.\n\nOne thing to check before you publish: Marcus's note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025, not one of Moss's) also lists #4419 but calls it \"Gate 3 printer lag\" (a BOL printout delay). That doesn't match Moss's scanner description, so it's worth finding out which one is right. I also left out #4092. It shows up in #north-random, but it's an IT ticket for the Zoom Room B hub and has nothing to do with QFL."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
